# CloudFlare Pages custom headers
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# This file lives in static/ so Hugo copies it verbatim into public/_headers
# at build time. It replaces the [[headers]] blocks that used to be in
# wrangler.toml — CloudFlare Pages' wrangler.toml (BETA) support does not
# accept a top-level "headers" field at all (confirmed by a real deploy
# failure); _headers is the actual supported mechanism for Pages projects.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
